<title>FRANCE: Framatome division wins British order.</title>
<headline>Framatome division wins British order.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's state-owned nuclear power station manufacturer Framatome said its Thermodyn division won an order from Britain's Interconnector Construction Company (ICC) to supply four compressors to the gas compression plant of Bacton, in Eastern England.</p>
<p>In a statement Framatome said ICC ordered four compression lines for a total amount of 200 million francs.</p>
<p>Each compression line includes one compressor supplied by Thermodyn and a gas turbine supplied by General Electric of the U.S.</p>
<p>A Framatome spokeswoman put Thermodyn's share of the contract at 60 million francs.</p>
<p>The four compressors are to be delivered in the fourth quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>ICC is a unit of Interconnector U.K. Ltd, a consortium that includes British Gas Plc, British Petroleum Co Plc, Elf Aquitaine, Russia's  Gazprom, Distrigaz, German  Ruhrgas, Amerada Hess Corp of the US , National Power Plc of the UK, and Conoco.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
